# Docker runtime

- Docker operations shell out to the host `docker` CLI; there is no Docker SDK abstraction. `docker.CheckDockerInstalled` is the only host check; Golem Deploy never installs Docker.
- `internal/docker` owns image listing/deletion and container lifecycle; `internal/volumes` owns managed volumes. HTTP translation belongs under `internal/handlers/docker`.
- Containers get the label `docker.LabelKey` (`dev.golemengine.deploy.label`, default `default`). `container.RunFromRequest` wraps `docker.RunContainer` and is shared by `POST /docker/container/run` and `POST /massrun/execute`. Containers currently run without a volume.
- Managed volumes are named `golem-deploy-<container>-data` and labelled `dev.golemengine.deploy.container` / `.created`; volume routes only see volumes with the container label. `volumes.CreateVolume` has no caller yet.
- `static_addons.go` validates and extracts static-store ZIP add-ons into a build context (see the static add-ons rule). No image-build route exists yet.
- Container request or response changes must be reflected in shared API types, mass-run presets, the web client, and `docs/API.md`.
- Verify with `go test ./internal/docker/...` (no Docker daemon required for unit tests).
